# Local Stacks

_Written by `beam local setup` from the installed CLI, so the option tables match it. Refresh it with
`beam local setup --only skill` after updating the CLI._

A **stack** is a named set of **steps**: Docker containers, builds, C# hosts, Scala services, the portal, this
workspace's microservices and portal extensions, and the local web package loop. `beam local run <stack>` brings
it up; `beam local ps`, `logs` and `stop` manage it from any terminal.

## Prerequisites
- A `.beamable` workspace (the portal repository, for the full stack) with the sibling repositories cloned:
  `BeamableAPI`, `BeamableBackend`, `BeamableProduct`. Setup finds `<Repo>_<suffix>` siblings next to a
  `<workspace>_<suffix>` folder first.
- Docker running.
- `beam local setup` done once on this machine (see **Setting up a machine**).

## Find out what this machine runs
Never guess step names, ports or folders: ask the CLI.
```
beam local run                         # the stacks, their variants and backends
beam local run csharp-portal --dry-run # the resolved steps, folders, ports, variables and checks
beam local ps --json                   # what is running now
```
`--dry-run` starts nothing. It warns when a stack misses something its steps need.

## Stack names
`beam local run <stack>[:<variant>...]`: variants apply left to right.

| Built-in stack | Runs | Backend |
|---|---|---|
| `full` | Docker deps, C# hosts, every Scala service, the portal, microservices, extensions, log forwarding | local |
| `backend` | Docker deps, C# hosts, every Scala service, log forwarding | local |
| `csharp-portal` | Docker deps, C# hosts, the Scala services they call and the ones login needs, the portal, microservices, extensions, log forwarding | local |
| `portal-extensions` | The portal, microservices and extensions | dev |
| `web-dev` | The local package registry, the portal, microservices and extensions (`:non-publish`: build the packages only) | dev |
| `remote` | This workspace's microservices and extensions, used from the hosted portal | dev |

Teams add stacks in `.beamable/shared/stacks/*.json` (committed); each developer in `.beamable/local/stacks/*.json`.
`beam local run` lists all of them with their layer.

| Variant (every stack) | Effect |
|---|---|
| `:build` | Rebuild everything the stack runs, changed or not |
| `:no-build` | Start without building, even when an output is missing |
| `:web` | Build the local `@beamable/sdk` and `@beamable/portal-toolkit`, publish them to the local registry, point the extensions at them, rebuild on every save |
| `:no-logs` | Don't forward logs to Grafana |
| `:local`, `:lan`, `:dev`, `:staging`, `:prod` | The backend (see **Backends**) |

Examples: `full:no-build`, `csharp-portal:web`, `portal-extensions:local`, `backend:lan`.

A build runs only when its output is missing or its inputs changed since it last built (git tree ids plus a hash of
changed files); otherwise the board says Up to date and why.

### Backends
One stack has one backend; beam steps get `BEAM_HOST/CID/PID` and tokens through the environment, the portal gets
`VITE_API_BASE`. The workspace's own login (`.beamable/config.beam.json`) is never changed.

| Target | Backend |
|---|---|
| `local` | This machine's stack (settings `host`). On first run the CLI creates a local org and realm (`--realm-*` options) with zones dev, staging and prod |
| `lan` | This machine's stack at its LAN address, for phones and other machines |
| `dev` / `staging` | Beamable's hosted backends; a remote login is asked for once |
| `prod` | Beamable's production; asks before every run (`--confirm-target` without a terminal) |
| an `http(s)://` address | Any gateway |

## Running
In a terminal `run` stays attached and shows a progress board until Ctrl+C stops the stack. **An agent always
detaches**, then reads the state with `ps`:
```
beam local run csharp-portal --detach
beam local ps --json
```
Running another stack name while one runs changes the running stack in place: steps the new name doesn't have stop,
new ones start.
