### Settings and variables
This machine's settings are `.beamable/local/stack-settings.json` (not committed): the step catalogue, `paths` (each
repository once, e.g. `"BeamAPIPath": "../BeamableAPI"`), `variables`, `targets`, `host`, `portalUrl`,
`logRetentionDays`. Steps refer to them as `${Name}`. Built-in tokens:

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| `${host}`, `${portalUrl}` | The backend and portal addresses |
| `${java}` | The JDK 8 home (`${java}/bin/java`) |
| `${maven}`, `${npm}`, `${node}`, `${dotnet}` | The toolchain's executables, or the bare command without one |
| `${logRetention}` | `logRetentionDays` in hours |

`--dry-run` lists every variable a stack uses and where its value comes from. After updating the CLI, refresh the
catalogue once with `beam local setup --only settings --force`; it keeps variables, targets and custom steps.

## Setting up a machine
`beam local setup` installs a private, pinned toolchain under `~/.beamable-toolchain` (JDK 8, Maven, .NET SDK, Node,
pnpm), writes the settings file, generates BeamableBackend's gitignored config files and checks the AWS
prerequisites. A second run only fills what's missing. Before it: install the .NET SDK and Docker,
`dotnet tool install -g Beamable.Tools`, clone the repositories.
```
beam local setup --quiet
beam local setup --only aws       # just the AWS checks
beam local setup --aws-guide      # the AWS setup guide for this checkout
```
Step ids for `--only`/`--skip`: `docker`, `jdk8`, `maven`, `dotnet`, `node`, `pnpm`, `settings`, `skill` (this file), `scala-config`,
`portal-config`, `aws`.

**Real AWS access is required.** The Scala `auth` service reads its JWT signing key from AWS Secrets Manager, so
without credentials every process comes up healthy and nothing can log in. `--only aws` checks the profile, the
services, storage and analytics roles, and the signing key, and names the fix (usually: add the developer to a
role's trust policy). `AWS_PROFILE` set to an empty string fails as "config profile () could not be found": unset it.
